msgstr "Søker etter eksisterende Sphinx-oversettelser i doc/source/locale."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:1
msgid ""
"Ensures rST underlines (===, ---, etc.) are at least as long as the "
"preceding text."
msgstr ""
"Sikrer at RST-underlininger (===, ---, etc.) er minst så lange som "
"oppfølgende tekst."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:3
#: readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.protect_rst:3
msgid "The rST text."
msgstr ""
"Det er en enhet som skal holde opp datamaskinene i den virtuelle verden av "
"Bitcoin og Ethereum."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:4
msgid "The rST text with fixed underlines."
msgstr ""
"_____________________________\n"
".. _underlines:\n"
"   | This is a fixed underlined text |\n"
"   \n"
"   The underscore character `_` can be used to create a fixed underlined text in reStructuredText (RST) documents. The fixed underlining is achieved by surrounding the text with double underscores on either side of the text.\n"
"\n"
"_____________________________"

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.protect_rst:1
msgid "Replaces rST-specific syntax with placeholders to prevent translation."
msgstr ""
"Erstatt rST-ekspedisjonssyntaks med placeholder-forhold for å forhindre "
"oversetting."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.protect_rst:4
msgid "A tuple containing the protected text and original constructs."
msgstr "En tupel med beskyttet tekst og opprinnelige konstruktioner."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.restore_rst:1
msgid "Restores rST-specific syntax from placeholders after translation."
msgstr ""
"Fjerner rST-specifik syktematisk sintaks fra håndjerninger etter "
"oversettelse."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.restore_rst:4
msgid "The list of original rST constructs."
msgstr ""
"**Original RST Constructs**\n"
"\n"
"* **Heading levels**: \n"
"    + `.. heading-level:: text`\n"
"    + `.. _heading-level: text` (note the underscore)\n"
"    + `.. {heading-level}:: text` (using curly braces)\n"
"* **Links**\n"
"    + `[text](url)`\n"
"    + `[text][id]`\n"
"        - `.. [id]: url \"alt text\"`\n"
"* **Images**\n"
"    + `[image][image-id]`\n"
"        - `.. [image-id]: image-path \"alt text\"`\n"
"    + .. image:: image-path \"alt text\"\n"
"* **Lists**\n"
"    + `+ Item 1`\n"
"    + `- Item 2`\n"
"    + `* Item 3` (unordered list)\n"
"* **Tables**\n"
"    + `` | Column 1 | Column 2 | ...\n"
"    + `` | --- | --- | ---\n"
"    + ... | ... | ... | ...\n"
"* **Definition lists**\n"
"    + `` :definition-name: definition-text\n"
"    + `` :definition-name: definition-text :definition-text\n"
"* **Footnotes**\n"
"    + .. _footnote-id: footnote-text\n"
"* **Inline formatting**: \n"
"    + `**bold text**`\n"
"    + `*italic text*`\n"
"    + `_underline text_`\n"
"    + `~strikethrough text~`"

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.restore_rst:5
msgid "The restored rST text."
msgstr "Original tekst er nå igjen."

